<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03BR">Remark <span data-tag="03BR">7.5.5.5</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a category, let $\overline{\mathscr {F}}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\triangleleft } \rightarrow \operatorname{QCat}$ be a categorical limit diagram of $\infty $-categories, and define $\overline{\mathscr {F}}^{\simeq }: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\triangleleft } \rightarrow \operatorname{Kan}$ by the formula $\overline{\mathscr {F}}^{\simeq }(C) = \overline{\mathscr {F}}(C)^{\simeq }$. Then $\overline{\mathscr {F}}^{\simeq }$ is a homotopy limit diagram. This follows by combining Example <a data-tag="03AD" href="/tag/03AD">7.5.2.8</a> with Remark <a data-tag="01HB" href="/tag/01HB">4.5.1.20</a>. </p>
